}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 On this day, the Celebrant begins the liturgy with the Salutation and the \softline
Collect of the Day.}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 Let us pray.\par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f1 Almighty and everlasting God, you hate nothing you have\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 made and forgive the sins of all who are penitent: Create and\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 make in us new and contrite hearts, that we, worthily\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 lamenting our sins and acknowledging our wretchedness,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 may obtain of you, the God of all mercy, perfect remission\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 and forgiveness; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 and ever.  }{\plain \fs24 \i\f1 Amen.}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 Old Testament}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20     Joel 2:1-2, 12-17,  }{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 or}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20  Isaiah 58:1-12 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 Psalm}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20     103,  }{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 or}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20  103:8-14 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 Epistle}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20     2 Corinthians 5:20b-6:10 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 Gospel}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20     Matthew 6:1-6, 16-21\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20   \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 After the Sermon, all stand, and the Celebrant or Minister appointed\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 invites the people to the observance of a holy Lent, saying}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20  }{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f1 Dear People of God: The first Christians observed with great\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 devotion the days of our Lord's passion and resurrection, and\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 it became the custom of the Church to prepare for them by a\par
}\column 
\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f1 season of penitence and fasting.  This season of Lent provided \softline
a time in which converts to the faith were prepared for Holy \softline
Baptism.  It was also a time when those who, because of \softline
notorious sins, had been separated from the body of the \softline
faithful were reconciled by penitence and forgiveness, and \softline
restored to the fellowship of the Church. Thereby, the whole \softline
congregation was put in mind of the message of pardon and \softline
absolution set forth in the Gospel of our Savior, and of the \softline
need which all Christians continually have to renew their \softline
repentance and faith.\par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f1 I invite you, therefore, in the name of the Church, to the\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 observance of a holy Lent, by self-examination and repentance;\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 by prayer, fasting, and self-denial; and by reading and\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 meditating on God's holy Word. And, to make a right \softline
beginning of repentance, and as a mark of our mortal nature, \softline
let us now kneel before the Lord, our maker and redeemer.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 Silence is then kept for a time, all kneeling.}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 If ashes are to be imposed, the Celebrant says the following prayer}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f1 Almighty God, you have created us out of the dust of the \softline
earth: Grant that these ashes may be to us a sign of our \softline
mortality and penitence, that we may remember that it is only \softline
by your gracious gift that we are given everlasting life; through \softline
Jesus Christ our Savior.   }{\plain \fs24 \i\f1 Amen.}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 The ashes are imposed with the following words}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f1 Remember that you are dust, and to dust you shall return.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 The following Psalm is then sung or said}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
